  "about": "Customs administration in Nepal is as old as the state itself. The modern Department of Customs, under the Ministry of Finance, administers the Customs Act and the Customs Tariff Act, collects customs duty, excise and VAT at import, enforces prohibitions and restrictions, facilitates legitimate trade, and publishes foreign trade statistics. Declarations are processed electronically through NECAS (Nepal Customs Automation System, based on UNCTAD's ASYCUDA World), which supports online declaration, risk-based selectivity, automated duty assessment, e-payment and post-clearance audit."
